What happens when this Java method is called?

```java
void awaitReady() throws InterruptedException {
    while (!ready) {
        this.wait();
    }
}
```

`awaitReady` is not `synchronized`, and no caller holds `this`'s monitor.

In Go:

```go
type Account struct { mu sync.Mutex; bal int }

func (a *Account) Balance() int { a.mu.Lock(); defer a.mu.Unlock(); return a.bal }
func (a *Account) Withdraw(n int) {
    a.mu.Lock(); defer a.mu.Unlock()
    if a.Balance() >= n { a.bal -= n }
}
```

